# TypeScript Standards

## Compiler Settings

- **Strict mode always on** — extends `packages/config/tsconfig.base.json`
- Target ES2022; packages use `NodeNext` module resolution
- API overrides: `commonjs`, `experimentalDecorators`, `emitDecoratorMetadata`
- Web overrides: `bundler` resolution, `@/*` path alias

## Imports

```typescript
// ✅ Workspace packages
import { OrderStatus, isValidOrderTransition } from '@byteagrox/types';
import { createOrderSchema } from '@byteagrox/validation';
import { db } from '@byteagrox/database';

// ✅ Relative within same package
import { StellarClient } from './client';

// ❌ Web importing backend-only packages
import { db } from '@byteagrox/database'; // in apps/web
```

## Types & Enums

- Shared domain types live in `@byteagrox/types` — do not duplicate enums across packages
- Zod schemas use `z.nativeEnum(OrderStatus)` for enum fields
- Prefer explicit return types on public service methods

## Error Handling

```typescript
// ❌ Silent catch
try { await fetchData(); } catch (e) {}

// ✅ Explicit errors with context
if (request.amountNgn <= 0) {
  throw new Error('Payment amount must be greater than zero');
}
```

Use NestJS HTTP exceptions (`BadRequestException`, `UnauthorizedException`) at the API boundary.

## Naming Alignment

- TS interfaces: camelCase fields (`farmLocation`, `createdAt`)
- Drizzle columns: snake_case in schema (`farm_location`, `created_at`)
- Keep enum values in sync between `@byteagrox/types` and `packages/database/src/schema/index.ts`
